texts.NASB95:
O God, the nations have invaded Your inheritance;
They have defiled Your holy temple;
They have laid Jerusalem in ruins.

texts.NKJV:
O God, the nations have come into Your inheritance;
Your holy temple they have defiled;
They have laid Jerusalem in heaps.

texts.ESV:
O God, the nations have come into your inheritance;
    they have defiled your holy temple;
    they have laid Jerusalem in ruins.

texts.NASB95:
Do not remember the iniquities of our forefathers against us;
Let Your compassion come quickly to meet us,
For we are brought very low.

texts.ESV:
Do not remember against us our former iniquities;
    let your compassion come speedily to meet us,
    for we are brought very low.

texts.NKJV:
Let the groaning of the prisoner come before You;
According to the greatness of Your power
Preserve those who are appointed to die;

texts.NASB95:
So we Your people and the sheep of Your pasture
Will give thanks to You forever;
To all generations we will tell of Your praise.

texts.NKJV:
So we, Your people and sheep of Your pasture,
Will give You thanks forever;
We will show forth Your praise to all generations.

texts.ESV:
But we your people, the sheep of your pasture,
    will give thanks to you forever;
    from generation to generation we will recount your praise.

texts.NASB95:
Oh, give ear, Shepherd of Israel,
You who lead Joseph like a flock;
You who are enthroned above the cherubim, shine forth!

texts.NKJV:
Give ear, O Shepherd of Israel,
You who lead Joseph like a flock;
You who dwell between the cherubim, shine forth!

Restore us, O God;
Cause Your face to shine,
And we shall be saved!

Restore us, O God of hosts;
Cause Your face to shine,
And we shall be saved!

Return, we beseech You, O God of hosts;
Look down from heaven and see,
And visit this vine

texts.ESV:
Turn again, O God of hosts!
    Look down from heaven, and see;
have regard for this vine,

texts.NKJV:
Restore us, O Lord God of hosts;
Cause Your face to shine,
And we shall be saved!

texts.NASB95:
I will hear what God the Lord will say;
For He will speak peace to His people, to His godly ones;
But let them not turn back to folly.

texts.ESV:
Let me hear what God the Lord will speak,
    for he will speak peace to his people, to his saints;
    but let them not turn back to folly.

texts.NKJV:
Preserve my life, for I am holy;
You are my God;
Save Your servant who trusts in You!

texts.NASB95:
Teach me Your way, O Lord;
I will walk in Your truth;
Unite my heart to fear Your name.

texts.NKJV:
Teach me Your way, O Lord;
I will walk in Your truth;
Unite my heart to fear Your name.

texts.ESV:
Teach me your way, O Lord,
    that I may walk in your truth;
    unite my heart to fear your name.

O God, insolent men have risen up against me;
    a band of ruthless men seeks my life,
    and they do not set you before them.

texts.NASB95:
Turn to me, and be gracious to me;
Oh grant Your strength to Your servant,
And save the son of Your handmaid.

texts.ESV:
Turn to me and be gracious to me;
    give your strength to your servant,
    and save the son of your maidservant.

texts.NASB95:
You have removed my acquaintances far from me;
You have made me an object of loathing to them;
I am shut up and cannot go out.

texts.NKJV:
You have put away my acquaintances far from me;
You have made me an abomination to them;
I am shut up, and I cannot get out;

texts.ESV:
You have caused my companions to shun me;
    you have made me a horror to them.
I am shut in so that I cannot escape;

texts.NASB95:
My eye has wasted away because of affliction;
I have called upon You every day, O Lord;
I have spread out my hands to You.

texts.NKJV:
My eye wastes away because of affliction. 
Lord, I have called daily upon You;
I have stretched out my hands to You.

texts.ESV:
my eye grows dim through sorrow.
Every day I call upon you, O Lord;
    I spread out my hands to you.

texts.NKJV:
I have been afflicted and ready to die from my youth;
I suffer Your terrors;
I am distraught.

texts.NASB95:
Do not hide Your face from me in the day of my distress;
Incline Your ear to me;
In the day when I call answer me quickly.

texts.NKJV:
Do not hide Your face from me in the day of my trouble;
Incline Your ear to me;
In the day that I call, answer me speedily.

texts.NASB95:
You will arise and have compassion on Zion;
For it is time to be gracious to her,
For the appointed time has come.

texts.NKJV:
You will arise and have mercy on Zion;
For the time to favor her,
Yes, the set time, has come.

texts.ESV:
You will arise and have pity on Zion;
    it is the time to favor her;
    the appointed time has come.

texts.NKJV:
I said, “O my God,
Do not take me away in the midst of my days;
Your years are throughout all generations.

texts.NASB95:
“Even they will perish, but You endure;
And all of them will wear out like a garment;
Like clothing You will change them and they will be changed.

texts.NKJV:
They will perish, but You will endure;
Yes, they will all grow old like a garment;
Like a cloak You will change them,
And they will be changed.

texts.ESV:
They will perish, but you will remain;
    they will all wear out like a garment.
You will change them like a robe, and they will pass away,

texts.NKJV:
For the mouth of the wicked and the mouth of the deceitful
Have opened against me;
They have spoken against me with a lying tongue.

texts.ESV:
He clothed himself with cursing as his coat;
    may it soak into his body like water,
    like oil into his bones!

texts.NKJV:
But You, O God the Lord,
Deal with me for Your name’s sake;
Because Your mercy is good, deliver me.

texts.ESV:
But you, O God my Lord,
    deal on my behalf for your name's sake;
    because your steadfast love is good, deliver me!

texts.NASB95:
Let them curse, but You bless;
When they arise, they shall be ashamed,
But Your servant shall be glad.

texts.NKJV:
Let them curse, but You bless;
When they arise, let them be ashamed,
But let Your servant rejoice.

texts.NASB95:
Keep me, O Lord, from the hands of the wicked;
Preserve me from violent men
Who have purposed to trip up my feet.

texts.NKJV:
Keep me, O Lord, from the hands of the wicked;
Preserve me from violent men,
Who have purposed to make my steps stumble.

texts.ESV:
Guard me, O Lord, from the hands of the wicked;
    preserve me from violent men,
    who have planned to trip up my feet.

texts.NASB95:
The proud have hidden a trap for me, and cords;
They have spread a net by the wayside;
They have set snares for me. Selah.

texts.NKJV:
The proud have hidden a snare for me, and cords;
They have spread a net by the wayside;
They have set traps for me. Selah

texts.ESV:
The arrogant have hidden a trap for me,
    and with cords they have spread a net;
    beside the way they have set snares for me. Selah

texts.NKJV:
Do not grant, O Lord, the desires of the wicked;
Do not further his wicked scheme,
Lest they be exalted. Selah

texts.NASB95:
“May burning coals fall upon them;
May they be cast into the fire,
Into deep pits from which they cannot rise.

texts.NKJV:
Let burning coals fall upon them;
Let them be cast into the fire,
Into deep pits, that they rise not up again.

Lord, I cry out to You;
Make haste to me!
Give ear to my voice when I cry out to You.

texts.NASB95:
Let the righteous smite me in kindness and reprove me;
It is oil upon the head;
Do not let my head refuse it,
For still my prayer is against their wicked deeds.

texts.NKJV:
Let the righteous strike me;
It shall be a kindness.
And let him rebuke me;
It shall be as excellent oil;
Let my head not refuse it. 
For still my prayer is against the deeds of the wicked.

texts.ESV:
Let a righteous man strike me—it is a kindness;
    let him rebuke me—it is oil for my head;
    let my head not refuse it.
Yet my prayer is continually against their evil deeds.

texts.NKJV:
But my eyes are upon You, O God the Lord;
In You I take refuge;
Do not leave my soul destitute.

texts.NASB95:
Look to the right and see;
For there is no one who regards me;
There is no escape for me;
No one cares for my soul.

texts.NKJV:
Look on my right hand and see,
For there is no one who acknowledges me;
Refuge has failed me;
No one cares for my soul.

texts.ESV:
Look to the right and see:
    there is none who takes notice of me;
no refuge remains to me;
    no one cares for my soul.

texts.NASB95:
I cried out to You, O Lord;
I said, “You are my refuge,
My portion in the land of the living.

texts.ESV:
I cry to you, O Lord;
    I say, “You are my refuge,
    my portion in the land of the living.”

Hear my prayer, O Lord;
    give ear to my pleas for mercy!
    In your faithfulness answer me, in your righteousness!

texts.NASB95:
For the enemy has persecuted my soul;
He has crushed my life to the ground;
He has made me dwell in dark places, like those who have long been dead.

texts.NKJV:
For the enemy has persecuted my soul;
He has crushed my life to the ground;
He has made me dwell in darkness,
Like those who have long been dead.

texts.ESV:
For the enemy has pursued my soul;
    he has crushed my life to the ground;
    he has made me sit in darkness like those long dead.

texts.NASB95:
I remember the days of old;
I meditate on all Your doings;
I muse on the work of Your hands.

texts.NKJV:
I remember the days of old;
I meditate on all Your works;
I muse on the work of Your hands.

texts.ESV:
I remember the days of old;
    I meditate on all that you have done;
    I ponder the work of your hands.

texts.NASB95:
Answer me quickly, O Lord, my spirit fails;
Do not hide Your face from me,
Or I will become like those who go down to the pit.

Let me hear Your lovingkindness in the morning;
For I trust in You;
Teach me the way in which I should walk;
For to You I lift up my soul.

Teach me to do Your will,
For You are my God;
Let Your good Spirit lead me on level ground.

texts.NKJV:
In Your mercy cut off my enemies,
And destroy all those who afflict my soul;
For I am Your servant.
